>  
> +	if (check_mul_overflow(max_pages, page_size, &max_length)) {
> +		rc = -EOVERFLOW;
> +		goto out_put;
> +	}
> +	if (length > max_length) {
> +		rc = -EOVERFLOW;
> +		goto out_put;
> +	}

This is some huge number, so big that this breaks the logic on 32 bits.

It just needs this:

+       max = length / page_size;
+       if (max > SZ_16M * BITS_PER_BYTE)
